# Loopback by default. A non-loopback host also needs
# CLOUD_DATABASE_ALLOW_REMOTE_HOST=1; compose sets it because the database is
# another container. Keep the default off for local processes.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/podhub?sslmode=disable
# CLOUD_DATABASE_ALLOW_REMOTE_HOST=0

# Listen address. Rust's CLOUD_BIND default is 0.0.0.0:8080 (src/main.rs).
# This skeleton defaults to 127.0.0.1:8080; the container image sets
# 0.0.0.0:8080 so the Caddy sidecar can reach it.
# CLOUD_BIND=127.0.0.1:8080

# Compose deployment (docker compose --env-file .env ...). The migration
# service is the only reader of PODHUB_API_DB_PASSWORD and
# PODHUB_WORKER_DB_PASSWORD; it sets the API and worker login roles before the
# application starts. POSTGRES_PASSWORD, PODHUB_API_DB_PASSWORD and
# PODHUB_WORKER_DB_PASSWORD are embedded in DSNs verbatim, so use only URL-safe
# characters (A-Z a-z 0-9 - . _ ~).
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-this-postgres-password
# PODHUB_API_DB_PASSWORD=change-this-api-password
# PODHUB_WORKER_DB_PASSWORD=change-this-worker-password
# CLOUD_INSTANCE_ID=podhub-prod-1
# PODHUB_SITE_ADDRESS=https://podhub.example.com
# CLOUD_COOKIE_SECURE=1

# Optional outbound DNS server for API and all workers. Empty uses system DNS.
# Database hostnames keep system DNS so Docker service names still resolve.
# Use a literal IPv4:port or [IPv6]:port; invalid settings stop process startup.
# UDP and TCP fallback use this server. Existing outbound address checks still apply.
# CLOUD_DNS_SERVER=1.1.1.1:53

# Password-reset mail. Use the browser-facing site origin, never the API bind address.
# Mail requires SMTP, the public site URL, and CLOUD_INTEGRATION_CONFIG_KEY (below).
# SMTP always verifies TLS certificates. No plaintext or insecure-TLS mode exists.
# Use starttls for submission (usually port 587), or tls for implicit TLS (usually 465).
# Username and password must either both be set or both be empty for a trusted relay.
# CLOUD_PUBLIC_URL=https://podhub.example.com
# CLOUD_SMTP_ADDR=smtp.example.com:587
# CLOUD_SMTP_USERNAME=sender@example.com
# CLOUD_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# CLOUD_SMTP_FROM='PodHub <sender@example.com>'
# CLOUD_SMTP_TLS_MODE=starttls

# Cloudflare Email Sending: onboard the From domain and use an API token with
# Email Sending: Edit permission. Sending to arbitrary recipients requires Workers Paid.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/email-service/api/send-emails/smtp/
# CLOUD_SMTP_ADDR=smtp.mx.cloudflare.net:465
# CLOUD_SMTP_USERNAME=api_token
# CLOUD_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# CLOUD_SMTP_FROM='PodHub <noreply@example.com>'
# CLOUD_SMTP_TLS_MODE=tls

# KEK for sealed store credentials. Required: without it key import answers
# "Seller 密钥托管未配置". 64 hex chars (or 32 raw bytes, or base64 of 32 bytes);
# any other string is hashed with SHA-256. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Changing it makes sealed credentials unreadable; keep the old value in
# CLOUD_SELLER_CREDENTIAL_KEY_PREVIOUS while rotating.
# CLOUD_SELLER_CREDENTIAL_KEY=
# CLOUD_SELLER_CREDENTIAL_KEY_ID=
# CLOUD_SELLER_CREDENTIAL_KEY_PREVIOUS=

# Shared encryption key for integration settings, user slice R2, and reset-mail outbox.
# Set the same value in the API and worker processes; use at least 32 characters.
# Preserve it across restarts: changing it makes existing credentials unreadable.
# CLOUD_INTEGRATION_CONFIG_KEY=

# Parsed once, only in internal/config. Spellings match the Rust source.
#
# OZON_WRITE_KILL_SWITCH (src/store/egress.rs is_truthy):
#   1 / true / yes / on  -> Seller writes disabled
#   unset, empty, anything else -> writes stay enabled
#   This process still does not send when writes are enabled.
# OZON_WRITE_KILL_SWITCH=1
#
# CLOUD_MEDIA_GC_DELETE:
#   unset -> purge enabled
#   1 / true / on / yes -> purge enabled
#   0 / false / off / no -> purge disabled
#   any other value, including an empty string -> purge disabled, process still starts
# A non-UTF-8 value is also invalid and leaves the purge off.
# Run worker-media-gc with this switch enabled to clear user slice prefixes.
# compose.yaml defaults this switch to 1 (production purge on).
# scripts/dev-api.sh defaults this switch to 0 unless explicitly set.
# In local development, DEV_MEDIA_GC_WORKER=0 keeps the cleanup worker stopped
# while allowing explicit file and folder deletion when this switch is enabled.
# CLOUD_MEDIA_GC_DELETE=0

# Legacy loopback test clients only; these do not configure user slice storage.
# R2_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:9000
# R2_BUCKET=podhub-slices
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Assets and private R2 storage are configured by the super administrator in
# 平台管理 → 系统存储桶. The credentials are encrypted in the integration snapshot.
# Production buckets are podhub-go-supplier and podhub-go-private. The public
# bucket uses https://podhub-go-supplier.ozon-pod.com; the private bucket has
# no public URL. Cloudflare access and CORS must be configured separately.
# 切片 R2 由工作空间所有者在设置中填写端点、桶、公开地址和 API 令牌，一空间一桶。
# 填写后立即用真实上传、回读、列举和删除验证，凭据加密保存。

# Load tests accept only Mode R (internal/loadtest). There is no other mode.
# PODHUB_LOADTEST_MODE=R

# Trace export (internal/platform/observability). Unset or blank: spans stay
# in process and nothing is dialed. A set value must be an http(s) URL on
# localhost, 127.0.0.1, or ::1, posted as OTLP/HTTP JSON. Any other value is
# logged and the exporter stays off; the process still starts.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:4318/v1/traces

# Official Seller routes, captured by API and all workers at startup.
# Unset/empty is direct. Use comma/whitespace-separated socks5h://host:port
# entries, followed by optional direct fallback. No URL credentials/path/query.
# The proxy resolves only the fixed official Seller hostname; environment
# HTTP_PROXY/HTTPS_PROXY are ignored. HTTP responses are never retried on fallback.
# CLOUD_SELLER_EGRESS_ROUTES=socks5h://seller-relay:1080,direct
# Managed sidecars consume config.json written by the admin relay controls.
# Missing config.json disables proxy use. When SWITCH_DIR is set, the sidecar
# must create its active marker only after applying the new config and listening.
# Switching/deleting/off removes that marker; a missing marker waits or uses the
# explicitly configured direct fallback. This Go process does not start sing-box.
# CLOUD_SELLER_RELAY_DIR=runtime/seller-relay
# CLOUD_SELLER_RELAY_SWITCH_DIR=runtime/seller-relay-switch
